# .gitignore for the project management pricing study
#
# THE RULE THIS FILE ENFORCES
# The six CSVs in data/ are the dataset and are committed by name. Anything
# else that lands in data/ stays out until it is added here deliberately.
# A denylist only protects you from the files you thought of.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything data shaped is excluded first.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.csv
scratch/
raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The dataset, named one file at a time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!data/frame.csv
!data/tiers.csv
!data/gates.csv
!data/volume_bands.csv
!data/addons.csv
!data/thin_set.csv

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output. The workbook is committed because it is the deliverable, but
# anything LibreOffice leaves behind is not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
~$*.xlsx
.~lock.*
*.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Any API key lives in an environment variable and nowhere else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
secrets.*
credentials.*
kaggle.json
.kaggle/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python and editors.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
env/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
